From 6d148b0dbb5b36b90ae16176063a860cc2e09ad1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:18:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: the devices that may wake the computer, one by one,
 Bluetooth too

Wake from sleep chose kinds of devices: the receivers of remote controls,
keyboards, or only the power button. A game controller or a mouse could
never wake the computer, a keyboard that Linux arms by itself could not be
kept from it, and Bluetooth was left alone, since arming its adapter would
let every paired device wake the computer.

System > Sleep > "Devices that may wake it" lists the input devices that
can wake a computer (hades-wake list), USB and paired Bluetooth ones, each
ticked where it may at the next sleep. What is ticked or unticked goes
into /storage/.cache/hades-wake-devices, "on" or "off" and the device's
key: a USB device by its IDs, with its serial number or its port where
another input device has the same IDs; a Bluetooth device by its address.
Only the changed lines are written (beside the file, renamed over it, read
back); hades-wake applies them at once, says what it did in the log of
Kodi, and a notification says how many devices may wake the computer
(34106 now counts every device, not only the USB ones). With "Only the
power button" the list is not offered: it says so.

The help of Wake from sleep no longer says that Bluetooth is left alone,
and the help of the list says what a Bluetooth device depends on (the
adapter keeping its power, the device connecting again by itself, an
adapter that cannot wake a computer at all) and how a device is
remembered.

Tested on the host (tools/regress/boot, stage wakesettings) with stand-ins
for Kodi and for hades-wake: the list, the labels, what is written, the
answers that change nothing, a list that cannot be read, no device that
can wake a computer. Not run in Kodi.
